    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAn exceptional A-rated, five-bedroom country home on approximately 1.16 acres (0.47 hectares), with beautifully styled interiors and sweeping countryside views, just a short drive from Dunshaughlin.\n\nProperty summary\n\nSherry FitzGerald Sherry proudly presents Dowsain Ghor, a distinctive country home combining generous accommodation, stunning interiors and a wonderful rural setting in Knockmark, Drumree.\n\nExtending to approximately 228 sq m (2,454 sq ft), this thoughtfully presented home stands on approximately 1.16 acres (0.47 hectares), with open lawns and far-reaching views over the surrounding countryside. Its attractive exterior, with stone detailing and a striking entrance door, gives the first indication of the individuality found within.\n\nThe entrance hall sets the tone, with decorative wall panelling, rich-toned flooring and an elegant staircase. Throughout the house, carefully chosen colours, contemporary finishes and beautifully considered details create a home of warmth and character.\n\nAt its heart is an impressive open-plan kitchen, dining and living room. Herringbone flooring draws the space together, while extensive glazing brings in natural light and connects the interior with the gardens. Classic kitchen cabinetry, a contrasting island and a stone-clad fireplace provide distinct focal points within this wonderfully sociable room.\n\nA separate sitting room offers a quieter retreat, while five bedrooms arranged across both floors provide flexibility for family life and visiting guests. Two bedrooms have en suite facilities, with a dressing room serving one of the ground-floor bedrooms. A utility room, boot room and bright landing with study space add to the practical appeal.\n\nAn A energy rating and underfloor heating complement the quality of the interiors. Outside, generous gardens, a detached garage and ample parking complete the picture.\n\nFor those seeking space, style and a strong sense of community, Dowsain Ghor offers a lovely country setting within easy reach of Dunshaughlin.\n\nSpecial features\n\n-Five-bedroom country home extending to approximately 228 sq m (2,454 sq ft).\n-Approximately 1.16 acres (0.47 hectares) with stunning countryside views.\n-A-rated energy performance and underfloor heating.\n-Beautifully styled interiors with herringbone flooring and an impressive open-plan living space.\n-Versatile accommodation with two en suite bedrooms and a separate sitting room.\n-Detached garage and ample parking.\n-Welcoming rural community just a short drive from Dunshaughlin.\n\nLocation\n\nDowsain Ghor enjoys a lovely country setting in Knockmark, Drumree, combining open countryside and a strong local community with the convenience of nearby Dunshaughlin. It is a location that allows you to enjoy the space and slower pace of rural life while remaining close to the town.\n\nDunshaughlin offers an excellent range of everyday amenities, including supermarkets, independent shops, cafés and restaurants, along with primary and secondary schools. Its library, sporting facilities and community organisations add to its appeal for families.\n\nThe surrounding Drumree area has a well-established community spirit, with local sporting life centred around clubs such as Drumree GAA, which caters for hurling and camogie. This sense of belonging is a particularly attractive aspect of the area for those putting down roots.\n\nFor commuters, the M3 provides onward access to the M50, Dublin city and Dublin Airport, while rail services are available from M3 Parkway at Pace. These connections make the area an appealing choice for purchasers seeking a country home within reach of the capital.\n\nGarden and grounds\n\nSet on approximately 1.16 acres (0.47 hectares), the gardens provide a wonderful sense of space and an attractive setting for Dowsain Ghor. Generous lawns extend around the house, complemented by established trees and boundary planting, with sweeping views across the adjoining countryside.\n\nThe open outlook is one of the property's most memorable features. Wide stretches of sky and views over the surrounding fields give the grounds a distinctly rural feel, while providing a beautiful backdrop to the principal living spaces.\n\nGlazed doors connect the open-plan kitchen, dining and living room directly with the garden, making it easy to move outdoors for summer meals, entertaining or a quiet morning coffee. There is ample room for children to play, alongside scope for keen gardeners to introduce further planting, a kitchen garden or additional seating areas.\n\nA generous surfaced driveway provides ample parking and circulation space beside the house. The small detached garage complements the exterior and offers practical storage for garden equipment, bicycles and outdoor essentials."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nA spacious entrance with decorative wall panelling, rich-toned flooring, recessed lighting and an elegant staircase with contrasting treads and white balustrades.\n\nKitchen/Dining Area - \nAn impressive open-plan space with herringbone flooring, large windows and glazed garden doors. Classic kitchen cabinetry, a contrasting island and pendant lighting define the kitchen, while generous dining and seating areas centre around a striking stone-clad fireplace.\n\nSitting Room - \nA separate reception room, ideal for reading, relaxing or entertaining away from the main living area.\n\nGround Floor Bedroom - \nA generous bedroom with adjoining dressing room and en suite, ideal for guests or those seeking ground-floor accommodation.\n\nDressing Room - \nDedicated dressing space adjoining the bedroom suite.\n\nBedroom 5/Office - \nCurrently arranged as a sitting room, with dark-toned flooring, neutral décor and tall windows. Equally suited to use as a bedroom, snug or home office.\n\nShower Room - \nLocated off the entrance hall, serving the ground-floor accommodation.\n\nBoot Room - \nA practical space with access from the entrance hall and outside.\n\nLanding - \nA bright landing with decorative panelling, a large window and space for bookshelves and a desk.\n\nMain Bedroom - \nA spacious bedroom with a separate closet and adjoining en suite.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nA well-proportioned bedroom suitable for family or guests.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nA comfortable bedroom completing the first-floor sleeping accommodation.\n\n"
      },
